ce each  other so I think those are things that  that would be good to keep in mind  I do have a few final thoughts  and you might say encouragement for you  as a self-directed student one of these  is something that I say to my students  and classes but I say to many other  people if you have enough support and  you approach things in the right way  anybody can study philosophy that  doesn't mean that you're going to  understand everything right away or even  at the very end but that's not the  measure of whether you're doing a good  thing by studying a classic  philosophical school or thinker or text  you do the best that you can you use the  resources that you have there's a lot of  things available I've contributed some  but many other people have contributed a  lot of great resources to helping people  understand stoicism and you make  progress and that's the key thing do you  understand more of epictetus after  putting in a couple weeks than you did  before that if so good you can build  upon that same thing with Seneca same  thing with Cicero same thing with Marcus  relia same thing with any of these  figures don't get too drawn into  worrying about whether you know people  or other people have got stoicism  completely right those debates have been  going on forever posted Onias himself  took a lot of heat from his fellow  Stoics back in his own time for being  unorthodox in important ways but it's  posted onus that we know anything about  and not that you know the Schmucks who  are criticizing him at the time stoicism  is really a valuable school of  philosophy not not just for applying  stuff but to understand the world of  ideas just as important as Plato or  Aristotle probably more important than  the Epicureans another one of the big  schools of the time so I hope that this  encourages you and empowers you to dig  into the stoic texts and you know just  make as much progress as you can you're  gonna start to see all sorts of cool  correlations on issues between  the Stoics and other thinkers and within  the stoic school itself so good luck and  I hope you get yourself some stoic text  whether it's buying them online or  buying them in a bookstore getting them  from library or you know finding them  somewhere in somebody else's library and  get to it  you
 

